E8534 `IN %s` binds a parameter where PostgreSQL parses syntax, so the statement never runs
 --> E8534.py:5:16
  |
4 | def bad(cr, ids):
5 |     cr.execute("SELECT id FROM res_partner WHERE id IN %s", [tuple(ids)])  # E8534
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
6 |     cr.execute("SELECT now() - interval %(days)s", {"days": "1 day"})  # E8534
7 |     query = "UPDATE res_partner SET active = false WHERE id in %s"  # E8534
  |
help: Build it with `SQL()` (a tuple expands, `SQL.literal` inlines) or pass a value the driver adapts

